#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:1
msgid "Release Policy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:3
msgid ""
"This page describes Mattermost’s release policy, and our recommended "
"practices around releases, including extended support releases, so that "
"you can allocate your IT resources effectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:5
msgid ""
"To ensure a secure, functional, performant, and efficient Mattermost "
"deployment, system admins managing a self-hosted deployment need to be "
"proactive in:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:6
msgid ""
"monitoring Mattermost release cycles and planning upgrades before life "
"cycles end,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:7
msgid ""
"considering the use of [extended support releases](#extended-support-"
"releases) for longer-term stability, and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:8
msgid "keeping both server and client applications updated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:11
msgid "Release Types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:13
msgid ""
"Mattermost releases include feature, extended support, and major "
"releases. Each release has a specified life cycle start and end date, and"
" life cycles depend on the release type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:15
msgid ""
"**Feature**: Feature releases contain new features and include high "
"severity and high impact security backported to the previous 3 monthly "
"releases. This is to ensure your organization's Mattermost deployment "
"remains secure and stable. It's crucial to apply feature updates to "
"maintain the security of your Mattermost deployment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:16
msgid ""
"**Extended**: Releases maintained for a longer period of time that "
"receive backports for security fixes and major bug fixes for the length "
"of their life cycle. Learn more about [Mattermost extended support "
"releases](#extended-support-releases) below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:17
msgid ""
"**Major**: Annual mid-year releases that follow a release theme, and "
"include multiple new features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:19
msgid ""
"With multiple release types, you can plan the upgrade path that best "
"suits your organization's needs and compliance requirements. Align your "
"plan with your organization's IT strategy and risk management policies to"
" ensure continuous operation without exposure to security "
"vulnerabilities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:21
msgid ""
"See the full list of all Mattermost Server and desktop app releases and "
"life cycles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:24
msgid "Extended Support Releases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:26
msgid ""
"Mattermost Extended Support Releases (ESRs) are a strategic choice for "
"organizations looking for stability and reduced frequency of updates. "
"Using ESRs can minimize disruptions associated with frequent upgrades, "
"making them an attractive option for environments where stability is "
"paramount."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:28
msgid ""
"Starting with the August 2025 Mattermost server and desktop app releases "
"(server v10.11 and desktop app v5.13), Mattermost has adjusted the ESR "
"life cycle as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:29
msgid "**Extended Cadence**: ESRs are released every 9 months."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:30
msgid "**Prolonged Support**: ESRs are supported for 12 months."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:32
msgid ""
"We strongly recommend planning ahead for upgrades before the end of an "
"ESR's life cycle to ensure continuity in receiving security updates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:34
msgid ""
"ESRs don’t include changes to product functionality or new features. ESRs"
" are intended for organizations who value stability over having the "
"newest features and improvements, or who have a long internal testing and"
" certification process to undergo when upgrading. Consider using ESRs for"
" more stable and long-term deployments, especially in environments where "
"frequent updates are challenging. If your organization prefers to have "
"the newest features and improvements, Extended Support Releases may not "
"be the best fit for you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:36
msgid ""
"To install extended support releases, follow our [install and upgrade"
"](/administration-guide/upgrade/enterprise-install-upgrade) "
"documentation. To restore a previous ESR, restore the database and "
"previous version if you need to revert an upgrade. Previous ESR versions "
"continue remain subject to a [life cycle end date](/product-overview"
"/mattermost-server-releases)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:39
msgid ""
"We strongly recommend reviewing [upgrade best "
"practices](https://docs.mattermost.com/administration-guide/upgrade"
"/prepare-to-upgrade-mattermost.html#upgrade-best-practices) for "
"upgrading, and [important upgrade notes](/upgrade/important-upgrade-"
"notes) for all the versions beyond the current ESR version you have "
"currently installed. See the [Mattermost v9 "
"changelog](https://docs.mattermost.com/product-"
"overview/mattermost-v9-changelog.html) for a list of database, API, and "
"`config.json` updates for all v9.x releases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:40
msgid ""
"Your license key is decoupled from the Mattermost server version, so you "
"can upgrade to the latest ESR using a legacy license. We highly recommend"
" working with your Mattermost Account Team to plan for a migration to our"
" new plans, and to access the latest features such as persistent "
"notifications, advanced compliance features, call recordings, and more."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:65
msgid ""
"**Timeline Legend:** The chart above shows both release dates and end-of-"
"life dates for each version. ESRs provide longer-term stability for "
"organizations preferring less frequent updates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:67
msgid ""
"🔵 **Blue bars**: Regular feature releases (monthly releases with standard"
" support lifecycle)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:68
msgid ""
"🔴 **Red bars**: Extended Support Releases (ESRs), released every 9 months"
" with 12 months of support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:69
msgid "v10.11 & Desktop App v5.13: Supported until August 15, 2026"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:70
msgid "v11.7 & Desktop App v6.2: Supported until May 15, 2027"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:73
msgid "ESR Notifications"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:75
msgid ""
"When an ESR is at the end of its life cycle, there will be announcements "
"ahead of time to provide time for people to test, certify, and deploy a "
"newer ESR version before support ends. After a release reaches its end-"
"of-life, no further updates will be provided for that version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:77
msgid ""
"To receive updates about Extended Support Releases, sign up for [our "
"mailing list](https://mattermost.com/newsletter/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:79
msgid ""
"For a new upcoming ESR, an email is sent out 3 months before the end of "
"support for an ESR version. This email includes a note about the new ESR "
"that was just published. A second email is sent out during the month when"
" an ESR version is reaching the end of support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:81
msgid ""
"For deprecated ESRs, an email announcement is sent 3 months in advance. "
"We also add reminders on our release announcements, changelogs, important"
" upgrade notes, and the [Mattermost Discussion "
"Forums](https://forum.mattermost.com/) site."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:83
msgid "Legacy Releases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:85
msgid ""
"The following table lists all releases across Mattermost v7.0, v8.0, and "
"v9.0, including ESRs. See the [unsupported legacy "
"releases](https://docs.mattermost.com/product-overview/unsupported-"
"legacy-releases.html) documentation for comprehensive changelog details "
"for these legacy releases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:88
msgid ""
"If you're on a legacy Mattermost release prior to v7.1, in order to take "
"advantage of newer Mattermost releases, you must upgrade to [v7.1 "
"ESR](https://docs.mattermost.com/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-"
"releases.html#release-v7-1-extended-support-release) at a minimum."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/release-policy.md:89
msgid ""
"Upgrading from one Extended Support Release (ESR) to the next ESR "
"(``major`` -> ``major_next``) is fully supported and tested. However, "
"upgrading across multiple ESR versions (``major`` to ``major+2``) is "
"supported, but not tested. If you plan to skip versions, we strongly "
"recommend upgrading only between ESR releases. For example, if you're "
"upgrading from v8.1 ESR, upgrade to the v9.5 ESR or the v9.11 ESR before "
"attempting to upgrade to the [v10.11 ESR](https://docs.mattermost.com"
"/product-overview/mattermost-v10-changelog.html#release-v10-11-extended-"
"support-release) or the [v11.7 ESR](https://docs.mattermost.com/product-"
"overview/mattermost-v11-changelog.html#release-v11-7-extended-support-"
"release)."
msgstr ""

